From 6abee38ef47c1f19b816657cb33d3bc7372f0d81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 10:30:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] subsys/pmci: add PLDM subsystem and DSP0240 Type 0 support

Add a PLDM subsystem that layers DMTF DSP0240 messaging on top of the
existing MCTP core. It is transport-agnostic: any binding registered
with libmctp (mctp_i3c, mctp_uart, mctp_i2c_gpio, ...) automatically
carries PLDM without further glue.

Key pieces:

  * include/zephyr/pmci/pldm/pldm.h      - public API:
      pldm_ctx_init(), pldm_register_type(), pldm_send_request_sync().

  * subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c              - core dispatcher.
      Registers as libmctp's rx_all callback; strips the MCTP type byte
      (0x01, PLDM per DSP0240 Table 1) and hands the message to either
      the responder (via a per-type handler table) or the requester
      (via an instance-id-keyed slot).

  * subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm_base.c         - Type 0 support.
      SetTID (0x01), GetTID (0x02), GetPLDMVersion (0x03),
      GetPLDMTypes (0x04), GetPLDMCommands (0x05). Encode/decode is
      delegated to openbmc/libpldm.

  * samples/subsys/pmci/pldm/type0_loopback - regression sample.
      Two MCTP contexts wired to an in-memory loopback binding
      exercise Type 0 requester and responder end-to-end. Runs under
      qemu_riscv32 and qemu_x86 in ~1 s.

  * west.yml                             - register openbmc/libpldm as
      a Zephyr module (pinned to df0a2219).

Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@example.com>
