+.. zephyr:code-sample:: pldm_type0_loopback
+   :name: PLDM Type 0 loopback
+   :relevant-api: mctp pldm_subsys
+
+   Exercise the DSP0240 Type 0 (Messaging Control and Discovery) commands
+   between a requester and a responder wired together over an in-memory
+   MCTP binding.
+
+Overview
+********
+
+The sample creates two Zephyr :c:type:`struct pldm_ctx` contexts sharing a
+pair of in-memory MCTP bindings whose ``tx`` callbacks cross-forward the
+packet to the peer's ``mctp_bus_rx()``. This lets the PLDM subsystem be
+exercised end-to-end without any hardware transport.
+
+The responder side registers the Type 0 responder from
+``subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm_base.c``. The requester side then issues:
+
+* ``GetTID``          - DSP0240 §9.2
+* ``GetPLDMTypes``    - DSP0240 §9.3
+* ``GetPLDMVersion``  - DSP0240 §9.4 (for the ``PLDM_BASE`` type)
+
+On success the sample prints ``PLDM Type 0 loopback OK`` and exits.
+
+Building and running
+********************
+
+.. zephyr-app-commands::
+   :zephyr-app: samples/subsys/pmci/pldm/type0_loopback
+   :board: qemu_riscv32
+   :goals: run
